  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-24 (in session): \"v20 with pohom, hodin 4/7 and siror 3, rest as recommended\". BUILD BOTH PARTS in a stable-id v20 bump. What was put to the owner (measured 2026-11-24 on dev fc8c8cb19, analyzer run directly, pre-split):\n- Part 2 reproduces. Cause read in the code: hypergumbo_core.analyze.c_family.c_family_parameters takes the text before the declarator, and its docstring says the * / & / [2] are left out on purpose. It is shared by C++, CUDA, HLSL and GLSL.\n- Wider than filed (fixture): n(int&&) / n(int&), k(int**) / k(int*&), m(int a[]) / m(int a), p(int (*cb)(int)) / p(int cb) tie; in part 1, r() & / r() && and q() volatile / q() tie as well as the const twins.\n- Real ties whose displayed parameters differ: binaryen/src 15 groups of 11,691 callables (pass.h PassRunner, wasm-interpreter.h Flow, wasm.h Expression::operator=, ir/match.h x9, support/name.h Name, ...), rocksdb/db 1 (compaction.cc sstableKeyCompare); 0 in libzmq, zstd, sherpa-onnx/csrc, envoy/source/common/http.\n- Cost, a PROXY (share of callables whose displayed parameter text holds * & or [): libzmq 39.7%, zstd 65.0%, sherpa-onnx csrc 48.0%, binaryen 55.3%, rocksdb/db 41.5%, envoy http 37.5%, pytorch native/cuda 69.2%. Part 1's cost was not counted.\nInstrument: session scratchpad cppcost.py (not kept)."  # 78ff
