  message: "DONE in PR #2370 (stable-id v20, merged 2026-11-24, dev 1acbf00b2). Both parts built.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-run on merged dev (analyze_cpp run directly, before the occurrence split; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/v20_11242026/closure/rerun_dev.txt):\n- This item's probe residuals/probes/cpp_pointer_overload/a.cpp (f(int) / f(int*) with a local struct L, g(int) / g(int&)): 4 tie groups when filed, 0 now.\n- This item's fixture guards/finam_fixture/b.cpp (c() const / c() with a local L): 0 tie groups of 39 symbols.\n- A wider fixture (k(int**) / k(int*&), m(int a[]) / m(int a), n(int&&) / n(int&), p(int (*cb)(int)) / p(int cb), d() / d() const, r() & / r() &&, q() volatile / q(), a const pure virtual, an out-of-class const definition): 0 tie groups of 36 symbols; each UNMARKED twin keeps the id it had on fc8c8cb19.\nRoot cause: c_family_parameters stored the text before the declarator as the type and the hash read only that; nothing read a member's cv- or ref-qualifiers. Fix: each parameter entry carries \"declarator\" (marks as written, names removed, layout-free), hashed beside the type; qualifiers go into the decorators slot and the local-scope label. C++, CUDA, HLSL, GLSL share the reader.\nMeasured (package, pre-split tie groups): binaryen/src 50 -> 19, rocksdb/db 29 -> 24, libzmq 14 -> 12, zstd 3 -> 1. 51-tree comparison: C++ 18,484 of 48,253 declared symbols moved, CUDA 1,978 of 2,768, GLSL 28 of 498; nothing else differs.\nOPEN POINT put to the owner, not built: nothing is evaluated, so m(int*) and m(int a[]), or const int a and int a, hash apart though C++ treats each pair as one function.\nNOT asserted: HLSL on a real tree (one tree, 0 of 20 callables moved; HLSL emits no member functions); ties from forward declarations and explicit specialisations (WI-rosog). Residuals are filed with the tag v20_residual.\n"  # e7d2
